=================== THE FOUR CHUNKS TOGETHER ===================

Against `main@origin` 41e5d8f1, the tree all four branched from — same harness,
21 interleaved paired rounds, `ident=Y` on every row:

    content         size preset  n  base_ms   cand_ms   ratio   speedup  p25     p75
    photo_cid       512  2      21  2463.530  2325.535  0.9442  1.059x   0.9416  0.9468
    photo_clic      512  2      21  2426.525  2286.334  0.9413  1.062x   0.9379  0.9450
    screen_terminal 512  2      21   666.313   641.347  0.9615  1.040x   0.9573  0.9636
    gradient        256  2      21   209.518   198.890  0.9480  1.055x   0.9445  0.9504
    gradient        512  2      21   460.980   442.223  0.9599  1.042x   0.9574  0.9611
    gradient        256  6      21    10.430    10.331  0.9914  1.009x   0.9683  1.0034
    gradient        512  6      21    33.853    33.752  0.9968  1.003x   0.9919  1.0017

A PRESET SWEEP on the photo at 512 (21 paired rounds each, ident=Y) —
including the one cell where the four chunks together are NEGATIVE:
    preset  6  1.022x  (span 0.9749-0.9814)
    preset 10  **0.996x** (span 1.0015-1.0093 — entirely above 1.0, so this is a
               REAL ~0.4 % slowdown, not noise)
    preset 13  0.996x  (span 0.9814-1.0100 — straddles 1.0; a null)
p10 and p13 are the `only_dct` regime, where the tx-type search has one
candidate: none of the four mechanisms has anything to remove there, and what
those presets pay is the owned-output wrapper's extra call frame and
`grown_out`'s `is_empty` branch (`txout_cshape_2026-09-05` reported the same
shape on the gradient and measured `#[inline]` on the wrapper as null-to-worse
at p2 — it was NOT re-tested against this photo p10 cell, which is the open
follow-up). In absolute time the trade is -137 ms at p2 and -1.6 ms at p6
against +0.054 ms at p10 on a 9.8 ms frame.

AND ON THE OTHER ISA. Every wall-clock number above is r7900x; the four
together were also measured on this Mac (M4 Pro, aarch64), gradient qp 40, 21
interleaved paired rounds, ident=Y: 256 p2 **1.049x** (span 0.9459-0.9592),
512 p2 **1.032x** (0.9616-0.9706), 256 p6 1.011x, 512 p6 1.008x. The box was
NOT quiet (load average 2.79, four users, other agents live), which is why this
is reported as a direction-and-span check on the second ISA rather than as a
position number.

A SIZE SWEEP of the four together (gradient, qp 40, preset 2, 15 paired rounds
each, ident=Y): 64 **1.051x**, 128 **1.051x**, 256 **1.055x**, 512 **1.043x**,
1024 **1.031x** — the gain is roughly flat in frame size and does not come from
a per-frame fixed cost.

and the instruction counts on the final tree against 41e5d8f1:
