=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED: the Ir on three contents; the wall clock on the four cells listed
at 21 paired rounds each; that the branch-free form equals the branchy one over
its entire reachable domain; that the `#[arcane]` dispatch variant is slower
despite fewer instructions.
ALSO MEASURED AND REVERTED, so nobody retries it: `#[inline]` on
`palette::palette_color_index_context`, the last out-of-line helper
`callcount_realimg_2026-09-04` item F named (2,961,716 calls / 211.6 M Ir =
1.5 % of a SCREENSHOT's preset-2 frame; C's `av1_fast_palette_color_index_
context` is `static inline`). The attribute DOES take — the symbol disappears
and the screen cell's Ir goes 14,003,946,792 -> 13,973,300,011 (-0.22 %, port/C
2.205 -> 2.200) — but the wall clock is a wash with a sign flip by content, 21
paired rounds each: `screen_terminal` 512 p2 **1.003x** (span 0.9951-0.9982,
entirely below 1.0) against `photo_cid` 512 p2 **0.999x** (span 0.9998-1.0032,
entirely at or above 1.0). A +0.3 % on screen content bought with a -0.1 % on
the dominant photo path is not a change worth its inlining risk, so it is not in
the tree. The 1.5 % that record quoted is the function's own WORK (~71 Ir per
call), not its call overhead; making it faster means changing the algorithm, not
the linkage.

INCIDENTAL, AND THE MOST USEFUL THING IN THIS SECTION: **BOTH open
screen-content correctness cells of `callcount_realimg_2026-09-04` are now
BYTE-IDENTICAL to C.** That record's "Open correctness finding" was
`screen_terminal` 512x512 p2 qp 40 at port 4,991 vs C 5,003 and `lineart_graph`
512x480 p2 qp 40 at port 3,087 vs C 3,098, both with IntraBC live, and it noted
that no existing screen gate runs qp 40 at p2. Re-measured here with the same
driver and the same prebuilt oracle:
    screen_terminal 512x512 p2 qp40   port 5,003 B = C 5,003 B   ident=Y
    lineart_graph   512x480 p2 qp40   port 3,098 B = C 3,098 B   ident=Y
(each verified twice — the identity pre-pass and the instrumented run's own
`.obu`.) They closed between that record and this one and NOT via the four perf
chunks of 2026-09-05, every one of which is byte-inert on 1,100 identity cells,
so the credit belongs to the screen/IntraBC work that landed on `main` in
between. Their port/C instruction ratios moved too, from that record's 2.206 and
2.444 to **2.200** and **2.385** — but those are not comparable as
before/after, because the earlier pair were ratios over DIVERGENT output and
that record explicitly refused to quote them as ratios.

NOT ESTABLISHED: that this is as fast as C's kernel — the alpha search is still
1.72x C's inclusive Ir, of which the per-alpha `tx_unit` half is already at
parity (385.7 M against C's 374.2 M, `callcount_realimg_2026-09-04`), so the
predict is still several times C's AVX2. A HAND-WRITTEN intrinsics kernel that
the inliner can still fold into the alpha closure is the untried next step, and
the variant above is the evidence that it must be inlinable to win. Also not
established: any preset but 2, any qp but 40, any size but 256/512, 10-bit
(`cfl_predict_hbd` untouched), the inter arm.
